      "vulnerability": {
        "@id": "https://ubuntu.com/security/notices/USN-8920-1",
        "name": "USN-8920-1",
        "description": "Several security issues were discovered in the Linux kernel. An attacker could possibly use these to compromise the system. This update corrects flaws in the following subsystems:   - Ethernet bonding driver;   - Network drivers;   - F2FS file system;   - Network file system (NFS) server daemon;   - Tracing infrastructure;   - io_uring subsystem;   - Networking core;   - IPv6 networking;   - IUCV driver;   - Netfilter;   - RxRPC session sockets; (CVE-2022-49149, CVE-2022-49170, CVE-2022-49182, CVE-2022-49201, CVE-2024-53187, CVE-2024-53210, CVE-2024-56763, CVE-2025-38724, CVE-2026-43456, CVE-2026-52910, CVE-2026-53131, CVE-2026-53221)",
